\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysian c.bank says rarely  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in ringgit  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Liau Y-Sing  \par \uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2007\par 10:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR, Feb 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has largely adopted a hands-off approach in managing the ringgit since it removed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg to the dollar, mostly leaving it to market forces to determine its level, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia freed the ringgit <MYR=> in July 2005 from its seven-year-old dollar peg in favour of a managed float, but economists and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the authorities had still kept a grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect its exporters.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Zeti Akhtar Aziz, who rarely comments on day-to-day management of the ringgit, told Reuters in an interview late on Thursday there had been minimal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  abandoned the peg of 3.8 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "At some points in time when there are excesses, this does occur but it has been very few in number," Zeti said.  \par \par \uc2 "For the most part, it has not required \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the rate has been market-determined. But we have been transparent in always mentioning that orderly market conditions are important and that our policy will be guided by that."  \par \par \uc2 The ringgit is one of Asia's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year, with a gain of about one percent.  \par \par \uc2 However, it defied expectations of a large, immediate appreciation when it was untied from the dollar in mid-2005, holding a tight range until early 2006, which raised suspicions of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased its tight grip on the ringgit last year, allowing more fluctuation.  \par \par \uc2 At the same time, they say, it has made its presence felt in capping sharp gains -- for instance, buying dollars through agent banks in January to prevent a rapid appreciation through 3.5 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Zeti said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step in when trading volumes were thin and market movements exaggerated.  \par \par \uc2 "Certainly, one of the criteria is if the market is very thin and a very small transaction results in a very large movement," she said.  \par \par \uc2 Philip Wee, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist with Singapore's DBS Bank, said Malaysia had loosened its hold on the ringgit on occasions.  \par \par \uc2 "After the Thai capital controls, they were keen to differentiate themselves from Thailand to build up investor confidence," Wee said.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the broad international push for more market-driven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , nobody -- except for Thailand -- would like to declare in a loud way that they are controlling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The ringgit traded at about 3.4920 per dollar on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 MALAYSIA-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|ABX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070223e32n000qo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
