\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysia Ringgit Up Late, Sets New 8-Yr High; Bonds Mixed  \b0\par\par\uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2006\par 11:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was higher late Wednesday versus the U.S. dollar, after achieving yet another new eight-year peak earlier in the day, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 As was the case with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the Singapore dollar, traders attributed the ringgit's rise to underlying dollar weakness.  \par \par \uc2 "Basically, the whole world is selling dollars, against ringgit and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader at a big local bank.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently to slow the dollar's decline, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market activities.  \par \par \uc2 "They were the only bidder in the market but they weren't very serious" about defending the dollar, said the trader.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zeti Akhtar Aziz indicated Bank Negara is comfortable with the ringgit's rise, saying its rise so far has been orderly.  \par \par \uc2 "Non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have strengthened across the board, so this in essence is an expected development," Zeti said in a Business Times daily report Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The word I use, stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , means that it's orderly; that the movement remains orderly, and orderly movement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is important," she said.  \par \par \uc2 The ringgit has risen nearly 4.9% so far this year against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 At 0830 GMT, the dollar was at MYR3.6070, far lower than Tuesday's MYR3.6140. It traded between MYR3.6050 - an eight-year low - and MYR3.6135 Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders remained confident the ringgit will extend its gains Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "I think tomorrow we will shed another big figure, and fall to the 3.59 level," said the chief dealer of a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Non-deliverable forwards declined, in line with the dollar's fall in the spot market. The one-month rate was MYR3.5930, down from MYR3.6000 Tuesday. The three-month rate was MYR3.5710, from Tuesday's MYR3.5760.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds were mixed in relatively narrow trading as investors focused on the ongoing sale of a MYR500 million seven-year bond by Germany's state-owned KfW (KFW.YY).  \par \par \uc2 The bond was indicated at a yield of 4.55% to 4.60%, about 30 basis points higher than notional seven-year Malaysian Government Securities yields.  \par \par \uc2 Short-term government paper, the focus of trading in the past few days, was also relatively inactive as investors preferred to participate in two tenders of government paper earlier Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold MYR500 million of three-month negotiable notes at an average yield 2.47% in an auction that drew a subscription rate of 4.4 times, higher than 2.3 times at the previous tender.  \par \par \uc2 A tender to sell six-month MYR500 million Bank Negara bills drew bids totaling 2.3 times the amount on offer, higher than the 1.4 subscription rate of an earlier auction. The six-month paper was sold Wednesday at 2.98%.  \par \par \uc2 The April 2011 Malaysian Government Securities yield rose 2 basis points to 4.14%, and MYR370 million were traded.  \par \par \uc2 The April 2009 Islamic Government Investment Issue yielded 4.00%, down 2 basis points, and MYR360 million changed hands.  \par \par \uc2 The Band 4, or 68- to 91-day, Bank Negara note yielded 2.31%, down 30 basis points with MYR346.6 million done.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Type of Instrument      Yield    Change from \par                                     Prev Close \par    April 2011 MGS          4.14%    Up 2 Bps \par    Overnight money rate    3.50%    Unchanged \par    3-month Klibor          3.75%    Unchanged \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Carolyn Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 603 2692 5254; carolyn.lim@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 03-05-06 0908GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1026 1851  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060503e253000ev\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
