\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysia Ringgit Hits Fresh High Late Vs Dlr; Bonds Quiet  \b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2006\par 10:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit achieved another new eight-year high late Monday as the U.S. dollar weakened against a host of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "(The dollar) is being sold by everybody," said the chief dealer of a local bank.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the dollar's fall was modest throughout the day, and absent once the U.S. unit fell below MYR3.6500, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Negara doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market activities, but traders say it tends to buy or sell small amounts of dollars throughout the day to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair stable.  \par \par \uc2 Late Monday, the dollar plunged against many other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Group of Seven industrialized countries' meeting.  \par \par \uc2 In a statement Friday, G7 nations made their strongest call yet for the appreciation of the Chinese yuan. Renewed comments by a number of central bankers suggesting plans to shift foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves further away from the greenback also weighed heavily on the U.S. unit.  \par \par \uc2 At 0800 GMT, the dollar was quoted, but not traded, at MYR3.6480, versus Friday's MYR3.6580. It traded between MYR3.6485 and MYR3.6565.  \par \par \uc2 Non-deliverable forwards mimicked the dollar's fall against the ringgit in the spot market. The one-month rate was MYR3.6370, lower than Friday's MYR3.6460. The three-month rate was MYR3.6190, less than MYR3.6290 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds were slightly higher in quiet and light trading ahead of Wednesday's monetary policy statement from Bank Negara.  \par \par \uc2 "(Malaysian Government Securities) are all quite quiet because of the (ongoing) consolidation and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting," said a bond trader.  \par \par \uc2 Bills and other short-term paper were buoyant, as offshore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators bought these assets with their newly purchased ringgit.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations require foreign parties who buy ringgit to use the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for purchases of assets such as fixed income, equities or real estate.  \par \par \uc2 The four-month Bank Negara bill yielded 2.77%, down 5 basis points, with MYR272 million traded.  \par \par \uc2 The April 2009 Islamic Government Investment Issue yielded 4.11%, down 4 basis points but just MYR140 million were transacted.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Type of Instrument      Yield    Change from \par                                     Prev Close \par    April 2009 GII          4.11%    Down 4 Bps \par    Overnight money rate    3.21%    Down 4 Bps \par    3-month Klibor          3.53%    Up 1 Bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Carolyn Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 603 2692 5254; carolyn.lim@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 24-04-06 0842GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1026 1851  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060424e24o000j5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
