\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysia Ringgit Up Late To Post-Unpeg High; Bonds Flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 09:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit rose late Monday to its highest level against the U.S. dollar since its July 2005 unpegging, as foreign players bought the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on hopes of further gains, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  emboldened speculators who kept up a steady flow of dollar-offers, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "Bids were muted today. There was no sign of the agent banks," said a trader at a midsized local bank. \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara, often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market via agent banks, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Negara doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market activities.  \par \par \uc2 At 0745 GMT, the dollar was at MYR3.6980, lower than Friday's MYR3.7040, after trading between MYR3.6980 and MYR3.7090.  \par \par \uc2 Non-deliverable forwards also fell, in line with the dollar's weakness in the spot market. The one-month rate was at MYR3.6900, lower than Friday's MYR3.6960, while the three-month rate was at MYR3.6760, from MYR3.6810 Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the dollar to fall to MYR3.6950 later this week, noting that the Chinese yuan - which the ringgit often shadows - remains in an uptrend.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia government bonds were quiet and traded narrowly ahead of February inflation data and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2005 annual report, both due Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Instead, "there (was) some (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign) exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 -driven interest on the bills," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The four-month Bank Negara note yielded 2.97%, down 5 basis points, while both the September 2016 Malaysian Government Securities and April 2011 MGS were flat.  \par \par \uc2 The September 2016 MGS yielded 4.12%, unchanged from Friday, while the April 2011 MGS yielded 3.74%, also flat.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Type of Instrument      Yield    Change from \par                                     Prev Close \par    April 2011 MGS          3.74%    Flat \par    Overnight money rate    3.25%    Unchanged \par    3-month Klibor          3.47%    Unchanged \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Carolyn Lim and E-Ling Liaw, Dow Jones Newswires; 603-2692-5254; e-ling.liaw@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 20-03-06 0832GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1026 1851  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060320e23k000ch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
