\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysian Ringgit Tests New Highs; Govt Bonds Unchanged  \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 09:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit extended gains Thursday to test new highs, buoyed by stronger regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and, in particular, the recent appreciation of the Chinese yuan, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Both foreign and local speculative buying pushed the dollar down MYR3.7080, traders said. That level marks a fresh post-unpegging high for the ringgit. Late Wednesday, the dollar was at MYR3.7090.  \par \par \uc2 "There's pressure for the dollar to drop further against the ringgit to catch up with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have strengthened more than the ringgit in recent weeks," said a trader with a large local bank. He said that MYR3.7050 would be the next support level for the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said that Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market through its agent banks to slow the ringgit's rise. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't typically comment on its market activities.  \par \par \uc2 At 0815 GMT, the dollar was at MYR3.7080 after trading narrowly between MYR3.7080 and MYR3.7108.  \par \par \uc2 Non-deliverable forwards held steady. The one-month rate was unchanged at MYR3.7000, while the three-month rate was flat MYR3.6850.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds were mostly flat in a cautious market after steeper-than-expected increases in retail fuel prices Tuesday, which investors fear could lead to higher inflation and more interest rate tightening, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Yields could have risen if not for a shortage of government bonds in the market, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The most actively traded April 2011 Malaysian Government Securities yielded 3.73%, flat from the previous day's close, with MYR405 million worth of the paper transacted.  \par \par \uc2 The December 2009 MGS yield was also flat at 3.45% with MYR106 million traded.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Type of Instrument      Yield    Change from \par                                     Prev Close \par    April 2011 MGS          3.73%    Unchanged \par    Overnight money rate    3.24%    Unchanged \par    3-month Klibor          3.46%    Up 1 bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Joseph Edwin, Dow Jones Newswires; 603-2692-5254; carolyn.lim@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 02-03-06 0847GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1026 1851  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060302e232000cp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
