\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysian ringgit at weakest since July de-peg  \b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2005\par 06:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 15 (Reuters) - The Malaysian ringgit on Tuesday eased to its weakest level since its peg against the dollar was abandoned in July, as outflows from local markets pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower.  \par \par \uc2 The ringgit <MYR=> <MYR=D1> fell to about 3.7815 per dollar, moving closer to the 3.8 level at which it was pegged to the dollar for seven years before the July 21 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 It has dipped about one percent since early August with further weakness prevented by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Second Finance Minister Nor Mohamed Yakcop played down the weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , telling reporters in Kuala Lumpur the ringgit levels reflected the strength of the U.S. dollar and that capital outflows were not a cause for concern.  \par \par \uc2 But dealers said disappointment with a lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation since the dollar peg was dropped meant foreign investors were likely to continue to exit Malaysia's bond and stock markets, keeping the ringgit under pressure.  \par \par \uc2 "Ahead of the depeg, a lot of foreigners had taken strong positions on the local markets and after the move they saw that there isn't too much \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation coming through," said Deutsche Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Mirza Baig.  \par \par \uc2 "A lot of positions taken up in the bond market have not been rolled over. Investors have been taking out their speculative capital from Malaysia and this has added to ringgit weakness."  \par \par \uc2 A dealer in Kuala Lumpur said expectations for rising U.S. interest rates would weigh on the ringgit.  \par \par \uc2 The key U.S. interest rate is at 4.00 percent and has been raised 12 times since mid-2004.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia's benchmark rate has been at 2.70 percent since it was introduced in April 2004, but some analysts expect a rate rise by the end of the year to curb inflation.  \par \par \uc2 "Interest rates in the U.S. are expected to continue to rise into the first quarter of next year and that in itself will fuel the outflows going into the end of the year," the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't see this trend of outflows reversing itself."  \par \par \uc2 He added that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to prevent the ringgit weakening beyond 3.8 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has led to a drop in \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which stood at $77.1 billion on Oct. 31 -- down 2.9 percent from $79.4 billion on Oct.14.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been in the market for the last two months," the trader said. "They won't allow the ringgit to touch 3.8. That won't look good four months after the unpeg."  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RINGGIT|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051115e1bf000bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
