\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ctrl Bk: Banks Urged To Curb Deposit Rate Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2003\par 07:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR -(Dow Jones)- Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zeti Akhtar Aziz reiterated Thursday that Bank Negara has asked commercial banks to make only minimal changes to deposit rates, following a cut in the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "We have urged banks to minimize adjustments (to deposit rates)," she told reporters after delivering a speech at an economic seminar. \par \par \uc2  Commercial banks are required to follow Bank Negara Malaysia guidelines in determining deposit rates which gives banks only limited leeway to tamper with rates. \par \par \uc2  Details on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's guidelines weren't available. \par \par \uc2  Zeti's remarks reiterate those in a statement from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Liquidity \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Negara Malaysia will ensure that the interbank rates are maintained at current ranges. This will minimize the adjustment to deposit rates," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday cut its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, used by banks to calculate their prime lending rates, to 4.5% from 5%, as part of the government's economic stimulus package. \par \par \uc2  Zeti later clarified that any change in deposit rates will be of a smaller magnitude than base lending rate adjustments. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted that the ceiling for base lending rates for commercial banks has fallen to 6% from 6.42%, and for finance companies to 6.94% from 7.46%. \par \par \uc2  Changes to deposit rates won't be of that magnitude, she said. Any decline in deposit rates "should be less than the adjustment in the base lending rate, which is around 40 basis points," Zeti said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Do not expect the one-month fixed-deposit rate to be below 3%," she added. At present, the average one-month fixed-deposit rate stands around 3.20%. \par \par \uc2  For other deposit rate maturities, adjustments won't be more than 30 basis points, Zeti said. \par \par \uc2  In the speech, Zeti dismissed concerns of a deflationary economy. \par \par \uc2  "Our policy is to promote consumption and investment activity ... (and that is) expansionary rather than deflationary," Zeti said in her speech. \par \par \uc2  She noted the country's interest rate cut will strengthen private consumption growth, which rose 4.2% in 2002 and is projected to rise 6.9% this year, and cited signs of healthy consumer demand. \par \par \uc2  "Therefore, we don't view our circumstances as a deflationary situation," she said. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the statistics department said consumer prices rose 1% year-on-year in April, continuing a benign inflationary trend seen over the past several years. \par \par \uc2  Turning to the U.S. dollar, Zeti reiterated the ringgit peg has served Malaysia well in mitigating external \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. \par \par \uc2  She noted that the dollar has depreciated against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to around the levels of when the peg was first introduced in 1998. \par \par \uc2  "The objective of our policy has never changed," she said. "We want the best mechanism that will facilitate trade and investment," adding that the peg continues to support significant amounts of both. \par \par \uc2  -By Monica Houston-Waesch,Dow Jones Newswires;603-2692-5254; nikki.houston@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Simon Harvey \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030522dz5m0008f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
