\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysian interest rates seen steady for now. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Syed Azman \par \uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2002\par 13:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Aug 15 (Reuters) - Malaysian interest rates are expected to remain steady in the near term although there is still room for a further cut, analysts and money market dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Talk of a lowering of \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate had surfaced in the market after earlier speculation that the U.S. Federal Reserve could slice another 50 basis points off the benchmark federal funds rate. \par \par \uc2  However, the Fed left the rate unchanged at 1.75 percent, a 40-year low, at its monetary policy meeting on Tuesday, but warned that economic risks have tilted toward weakness in a step that may foreshadow rate reductions ahead. \par \par \uc2  "There is no pressing need for a rate cut at this point. Any cut would send a confusing signal to the market,"Suresh Kumar, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with Standard & Poor's/MMS, said of Malaysian rates. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara last cut its three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to 5.0 percent on September 20, days after the September 11 attacks on the United States that jolted global markets. \par \par \uc2  Anthony Dass, head of research at SJ Securities, said with the inflation rate still benign, the current accommodative monetary policy was expected to remain intact. \par \par \uc2  "This means the 5.0 percent slapped on the three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate will remain," he said. \par \par \uc2  A cut in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate would also hurt bank profits, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "We estimate that bank earnings would decline by about 5.0 percent for every 50 basis point reduction in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate," said one banking analyst. \par \par \uc2  ROOM FOR RATE CUT \par \par \uc2  But analysts did not rule out lower interest rates going forward if the United States cut rates by another 50 basis points and if the weak external economic outlook was prolonged. \par \par \uc2  "Bank Negara is looking at U.S. rates for an indication on domestic interest rates. Based on the current domestic and offshore interest rates, we believe there is room for some revision," said Franklin Tan, head of research at OCBC Securities in Malaysia. \par \par \uc2  "Secondly, the gap between domestic interbank rates and the present \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is still rich at 180 basis points. As such, there is a strong possibility of a 50 basis point cut." \par \par \uc2  The benchmark three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (KLIBOR) currently stands at 3.24 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate was introduced in September 1998 to rein in runaway interest rates, which reached as high as 18 percent at the height of the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  As the base lending rate (BLR) is pegged to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, a 50 basis point rate cut will lower the BLR for banks to a new all-time low of six percent from the current 6.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  Banks' net interest income margins will be squeezed as liabilities are locked at higher rates and cannot be re-priced immediately. \par \par \uc2  Deposit rates range between 3.20 percent and 4.0 percent for a period spanning one month to one year. \par \par \uc2  Thus banks with a high proportion of floating rate loans and high loan-deposit ratios could be hard hit. They include Commerce Asset and RHB Bank. \par \par \uc2  But top lender Malayan Banking would be among those least affected, OCBC's Tan said. \par \par \uc2  Money market dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could also be looking for other ways to lower borrowing costs to keep rates steady given the excess liquidity in the banking system. \par \par \uc2  Options included reverting back to using the three-month KLIBOR in determining the base lending rate instead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, they said. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said such a move was unlikely as it would result in a big drop in interest rates given the 176 basis point differential between KLIBOR and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020815dy8f00lgi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
