\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia sees inflation at about 1.8 pct in 2000. \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2000\par 04:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANDAR SERI BEGAWAN, Sept 10 (Reuters) - Malaysia's inflation rate is likely to dip to about 1.8 percent in 2000 from 2.8 percent last year, despite a proposed hike in petroleum prices, Deputy Finance Minister Shafie Salleh said on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  "Based on present trends, it is anticipated that the inflation rate would be about 1.8 percent in 2000 as a whole, considering that excess capacity still exists in the economy and monetary policy continues to be accomodative to support economic growth," Shafie told Reuters in an interview in Brunei. \par \par \uc2  Shafie is leading the Malaysian delegation at the seventh APEC finance ministers meeting in the oil-rich sultanate. \par \par \uc2  The minister said bank lending rates could be kept low in the near term as the inflationary outlook remained subdued. \par \par \uc2  "As monetary policy will continue to remain accomodative to firmly support growth, it is likely that the 3-month BNM (Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate will remain at the current 5.5 percent," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara's three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is used by banks and financial institutions as a benchmark to set their prime lending rates. \par \par \uc2  Shafie said the economy, spurred by strong exports and buoyant domestic demand, was likely to expand more than the official estimate of 5.8 percent in the current year. He said there was no need to adjust the two-year-old ringgit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, which was in line with economic fundamentals and benefitted the economy. \par \par \uc2  "Currently, the degree of undervaluation is very small and the stable exchange rate has a positive impact on economic activity," he said. \par \par \uc2  "However, if circumstances occur which cause a gross misalignment of the ringgit exchange rate, then Bank Negara Malaysia will, of course respond accordingly." \par \par \uc2  Malaysia imposed capital controls and pegged its ringgit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 3.8 to the U.S. dollar in September 1998 to stem the outflow of short-term capital during the Asian economic crisis in 1997-98. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9a08kwc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
