\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals regain ground with yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 861 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 1999\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0900 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared early losses as \par \par \uc2  the yen recovered some ground on growing talk Japan might have \par \par \uc2  to consider an extra budget for fiscal 1999/2000. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the speculation stemmed in part from a report \par \par \uc2  by a U.S. consulting firm saying Japan may have to compile an \par \par \uc2  extra budget, but a senior Liberal Democratic Party official \par \par \uc2  dismissed the talk. \par \par \uc2      "That's ridiculous. The fiscal year has just started," \par \par \uc2  Yukihiko Ikeda, LDP policy chief said. \par \par \uc2      Earlier in the day, Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said \par \par \uc2  his ministry was not considering additional fiscal stimulus in \par \par \uc2  the light of the latest "tankan" survey of corporate sentiment \par \par \uc2  and severe job conditions. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said dollar selling intensified as long positions \par \par \uc2  had accumulated from an overnight surge in New York. \par \par \uc2      "In a way the report was a good excuse for those who were \par \par \uc2  eager to cut dollar long positions that had been piling up from \par \par \uc2  the overnight rally," a trust bank dealer in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** The Philippine peso\tab     bounced back, supported by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remittances from overseas workers received over the Easter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par break and data showing inflation was on the decline thanks to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more stable food prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government said March consumer prices were up only 8.7\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent on a year earlier, compared with the 9.9 percent annual\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise seen in February.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It was the lowest annual inflation rate recorded since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par March 1998 and analysts said it would provide a platform for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to further ease interest rates and perhaps cut\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank reserve requirements.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *** The Taiwan dollar\tab   was unmoved by news the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consumer price index in March was down 0.46 percent on a year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier, contrary to expectations of a modest rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wholesale prices fell 5.83 percent in the same period.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A statistics bureau official reiterated the state view that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan faced "no deflationary pressure" despite the surprise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par March CPI downturn, saying rises in world energy prices were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fuelling some inflationary pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *** The rupiah\tab   slipped on offshore dollar demand,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wiping out recent gains fuelled by an improving inflation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par picture and news of a debt rescheduling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the rupiah tended to find support whenever\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia received a fresh injection of aid money, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continuing political and economic uncertainty soon capped the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Indonesia Managing Director Miranda Goeltom said she\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par saw lower interest rates ahead after the latest figures showing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the consumer price index fell 0.18 percent between February and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** The Korean won\tab     was flat as dollar offers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par countered the impact of a weak yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Provisional finance ministry figures showed South Korea\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par received $2.0 billion worth of foreign direct investment plans\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the first quarter, up sharply from $572 million in the same\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par period a year ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** The Indian rupee\tab     fell sharply in the face of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's deteriorating political situation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said they were on guard for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the rupee fell from an opening at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 42.445/465.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The decline accelerated on dwindling prospects that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hindu nationalist government's partner, the AIADMK, would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decide to stay in the ruling coalition.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** Bank Negara \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its three-month \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate to 6.5 percent from 7.0 percent late on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It said the maximum base lending rates of commercial banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were expected to drop to 7.67 percent from 8.04 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last cut the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par benchmark for commercial bank lending, on November 10 when it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was lowered to 7.00 percent from 7.5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The latest rate cut was not unexpected as interbank rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have been falling over the past few days due to excess\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par liquidity in the money market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The bank said the latest cut reflects the downward trend in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the inflation rate, which it projected would fall below four\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent this year from 5.3 percent in 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** Malaysian business groups said the ringgit was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par undervalued at 3.80 to the dollar and could make imports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expensive and debt servicing burdensome.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Leading trade associations urged Trade Minister Rafidah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Aziz to adjust the ringgit exchange rate, saying an upward\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par revision would also give a psychological boost to investors.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day TUE 06 0854GMT\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000..........0.01%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Rupiah......8685.00......8665.00.........-0.23%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Baht..........37.85........37.68.........-0.45%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Peso..........38.42........38.52..........0.26%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sing dlr.....1.7360.......1.7335.........-0.14%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Taiwan dlr...3