\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals soft as yen droops. \b0\par\par\uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 1999\par 03:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0030 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were looking soft in \par \par \uc2  early trade with the yen still depressed against the dollar but \par \par \uc2  off its worst on light profit-taking. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the dollar showed potential to trade higher in \par \par \uc2  the near term, with firm support expected around 121 yen. \par \par \uc2      U.S. stock prices surged overnight, signalling new investor \par \par \uc2  confidence in America's robust economy and sparking dollar \par \par \uc2  buying. \par \par \uc2      Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said Monday's \par \par \uc2  "tankan" survey of business sentiment showed the worst is over \par \par \uc2  for the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2      *** Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  rate to 6.5 percent from 7.0 percent late on Monday. \par \par \uc2      It said the maximum base lending rates of commercial banks \par \par \uc2  were expected to drop to 7.67 percent from 8.04 percent. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last cut the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, the \par \par \uc2  benchmark for commercial bank lending, on November 10 when it \par \par \uc2  was lowered to 7.00 percent from 7.5 percent. \par \par \uc2      The latest rate cut was not unexpected as interbank rates \par \par \uc2  have been falling over the past few days due to excess \par \par \uc2  liquidity in the money market. \par \par \uc2      The bank said the latest cut reflects the downward trend in \par \par \uc2  the expected inflation rate and is also aimed at sustaining \par \par \uc2  positive developments in the economy. \par \par \uc2      It said last week the consumer price index was expected to \par \par \uc2  fall below four percent this year from 5.3 percent in 1998. \par \par \uc2      *** Malaysian business groups said the ringgit was \par \par \uc2  undervalued at 3.80 to the dollar and could make imports \par \par \uc2  expensive and debt servicing burdensome. \par \par \uc2      Leading trade associations urged Trade Minister Rafidah \par \par \uc2  Aziz to adjust the ringgit exchange rate, saying an upward \par \par \uc2  revision would also give a psychological boost to investors. \par \par \uc2      *** The peso was steady after gaining ground from dollar \par \par \uc2  inflows on Monday. \par \par \uc2      Finance Secretary Edgardo Espiritu said the Philippines \par \par \uc2  received $1.03 billion in loans from Japan and funds from bond \par \par \uc2  issues in March. \par \par \uc2      He also said the benchmark 91-day Treasury bill rate may \par \par \uc2  fall below 11 percent in April if inflation declines further. \par \par \uc2      March inflation data is due at 0100 GMT. \par \par \uc2      A Reuters poll of five economists last month showed \par \par \uc2  inflation could drop to 9.28 percent in March from February's \par \par \uc2  9.9 percent. \par \par \uc2      Moody's Investors Service said overnight the Philippines' \par \par \uc2  stable foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ratings outlook reflects recent \par \par \uc2  improvements in the balance of payments and external payments \par \par \uc2  position as well as past progress in fiscal adjustment and \par \par \uc2  structural reform. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won opened lower after a three-day break as \par \par \uc2  the market played catch-up with a weaker yen. \par \par \uc2      But Seoul shares made strong headway on persistent \par \par \uc2  institutional buying of blue chips. \par \par \uc2      The Finance Ministry said on Monday the number of Korean \par \par \uc2  companies forced to close their bank accounts after defaulting \par \par \uc2  on debt rose to 656 in March from 555 in February. \par \par \uc2      It said the increase was mainly due to a higher number of \par \par \uc2  new start-ups and noted that the debt default ratio was still \par \par \uc2  low compared with last year. \par \par \uc2      The number of firms in default on debt reached a peak of \par \par \uc2  1,226 in January 1998. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day TUE 06 0056GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8550.00......8665.00.........1.35% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.70........37.68........-0.05% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.50........38.52.........0.05% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7345.......1.7335........-0.06% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...33.100.......33.100.........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1225.50......1223.00........-0.20% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....121.54.......120.63........-0.75% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8550.00......2432.00........-71.56% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.68........25.90........-31.26% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.50........26.50........-31.17% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7345.......1.4300........-17.56% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..33.1000......27.7500........-16.16% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1225.50.......842.00........-31.29% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....121.54.......114.40........-5.87% \par \par \uc2   - Asia \b \highl