\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals wilting, Sing dlr downcast. \b0\par\par\uc2 787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 06:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2     0420 GMT - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were tending to droop despite \par \par \uc2  the dollar sliding below 138 yen as fears of another missile \par \par \uc2  strike by North Korea and Malaysia's retreat from world markets \par \par \uc2  turned investors off the region. \par \par \uc2      Dollar/yen was off its lows below the 137 level, but making \par \par \uc2  slow progress after Japan's "Mr Yen", Eisuke Sakakibara said \par \par \uc2  the yen's excessive weakness had not yet fulling corrected and \par \par \uc2  a senior Finance Ministry official said Japan was ready to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. \par \par \uc2      *** \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's radical new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls \par \par \uc2  continued to cast a shadow over the region, with the shock \par \par \uc2  sacking of Deputy Prime Minister and Finance Minister Anwar \par \par \uc2  Ibrahim late on Wednesday, deepening the market's gloom. \par \par \uc2      Anwar, seen as one of the last market-friendly members of \par \par \uc2  the Malaysian government, is due to hold a news conference at \par \par \uc2  0700 GMT. \par \par \uc2      Some analysts say his removal means the cabinet is now \par \par \uc2  united behind Prime Minister Mahathir, and likely to have more \par \par \uc2  success in implementing current policy. \par \par \uc2      The Malaysian government is due to hold an emergency \par \par \uc2  Cabinet meeting to name Anwar's successor today. \par \par \uc2      Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara, eased monetary policy \par \par \uc2  further by cutting its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate (the three-month \par \par \uc2  interbank rate) to eight percent from 9.5 percent. \par \par \uc2      It said it expects the maximum base lending rate of \par \par \uc2  commercial banks and finance companies to moderate to 9.06 \par \par \uc2  percent and 10.76 percent, respectively, following the \par \par \uc2  reduction in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  The liquid asset ratio of commercial banks will also be \par \par \uc2  reduced to 15 percent from 17 percent of total eligible \par \par \uc2  liabilities from September 16 and commercial banks will no \par \par \uc2  longer be required to maintain vostro balances of foreign \par \par \uc2  banking institutions with Bank Negara from Thursday. A vostro \par \par \uc2  account is a foreign bank's account maintained in a domestic \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Ringgit forward markets were still trying to unravel \par \par \uc2  positions ahead of the complete end to offshore trading in the \par \par \uc2  ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara said in a circular to chiefs of banks that it \par \par \uc2  would introduce mechanisms to allow for settlement of \par \par \uc2  outstanding ringgit transactions after September 9. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Bank Negara said the ringgit's exchange rate \par \par \uc2  would be fixed at 3.80 to the dollar for an indefinite period, \par \par \uc2  but dealers said there was already talk of a black market, with \par \par \uc2  the dollar being quoted above 4.50 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  "The Malaysian government is taking a lot of risk by fixing \par \par \uc2  the exchange rate," the head of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a \par \par \uc2  European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  *** Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market Committee has \par \par \uc2  agreed on a rate of four Malaysian ringgit to one U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  for the settlement of outstanding ringgit positions in the \par \par \uc2  offshore market. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was among the biggest losers in the \par \par \uc2  region, falling within a whisker of the 1.78 level from a \par \par \uc2  morning high of 1.75, as players sold it as a proxy for the now \par \par \uc2  untradeable ringgit and illiquid baht and rupiah. \par \par \uc2      "Everybody just wants to catch hold of dollars at the \par \par \uc2  moment.wants to buy," the European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2      He said the Sing dollar had also been hit by speculation \par \par \uc2  that oil-rich Brunei might abandon its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  link with \par \par \uc2  Singapore, but added that this seemed unlikely in the current \par \par \uc2  volatile environment. \par \par \uc2      *** The Philippine peso slipped on dollar demand from \par \par \uc2  companies for foreign debt payments. \par \par \uc2      The government said merchandise exports rose 19 percent in \par \par \uc2  the first seven months of 1998, compared with a year ago. \par \par \uc2      Exports rose 20.9 percent year-on-year in July. \par \par \uc2      Budget Secretary Benjamin Diokno said the IMF had expressed \par \par \uc2  concern over whether the government can meet its revenue goals. \par \par \uc2      The government has projected a deficit of 40 billion pesos \par \par \uc2  for the year, but Manila newspapers said the IMF expected a \par \par \uc2  higher deficit of 50 billion pesos. \par \par \uc2      Change on the day THU 03 0427GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest.....Prev Close...Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit....3.80.........3.80.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.....10650.00.....10500.00....-1.41% \par \par \uc2   Baht.......40.73........40.70.......-0.07% \par \par \uc2   Peso.......43.62........43.33.......-0.66% \par \par \uc2   Sing Dlr...1.76.........1.75........-0.51% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan Dlr.34.77........34.77........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Korean Won.1332.00......1339.00......0.53% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest.....July '97.....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit....3.80.........2.52.......-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.....10650.00.....2432.00....-77.16% \par \par \uc2   Baht.......40.73........25.90......-36.41% \par \par \uc2   Peso.......43.62........26.50......-39.25% \par \par \uc2   Sing Dlr...1.76.........1.43.......-18.70% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan Dlr.34.77........27.75......-20.19% \par \par \uc2   Korean Won.1332.00......842.00.....-36.79% \par \par \uc2  - Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840 \par \par \uc2  - Email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du93023op\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
