\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia moves to cut interest rates again. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Reme Ahmad \par \uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 16:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Malaysia, Sept 3 (Reuters) - Malaysia cut interest rates again Thursday, barely 24 hours after dismissing its finance minister, who had favoured keeping rates high, and two days after imposing tough \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said it eased monetary policy by cutting its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, which serves as a benchmark for commercial bank lending, to 8.0 percent from 9.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The easing was the fourth reduction in the rate in the past month as part of a government plan to revive the recession-hit economy. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara said it expects the maximum base lending rate of commercial banks and finance companies to moderate to 9.06 percent and 10.76 percent, respectively. The key base lending rate quoted by the country's biggest bank, Malayan Banking Bhd, is currently at 10.3 percent, after it sharply reduced the rate from 10.9 percent from Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said the liquid asset ratio of commercial banks will be reduced to 15 percent from 17 percent of total eligible liabilities from Sept. 16. Dealers said the move will bring down banks' cost of funds. \par \par \uc2  The rate cut came barely 24 hours after the dismissal of Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim by Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad, who had repeatedly blamed high interest rates for the sharp contraction of the economy. \par \par \uc2  Malaysian gross domestic product shrank by 6.8 percent in the second quarter of this year from the year-earlier period, sinking the country into its first recession in 13 years. The economy contracted by 2.8 percent in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  Anwar's ouster followed the double resignations of Bank Negara's governor and deputy governor last week over differences with Mahathir on how to manage the economy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Malaysia has room to lower interest rates after shielding its ringgit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from fluctuations by imposing controls on the convertibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Expectations of a big inflow of ringgit from offshore accounts would also allow for the lowering of interest rates, they said. \par \par \uc2  Mahathir said Tuesday that ringgit notes must be brought home by the end of this month, making the ringgit held outside Malaysia worthless as of Oct. 1. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du93023ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
