\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia seen cutting rates further to spur growth. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Syed Azman \par \uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1998\par 13:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Aug 4 (Reuters) - Malaysia is likely to cut interest rates further this year in a bid to keep the economy from sliding deeper into recession, analysts said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts expect the key three-month interbank rate to fall by another 100 to 200 basis points by the end of the year, from around 10.5 percent now. \par \par \uc2  "Overall, the environment is relatively conducive for rate cuts," said Simon Flint, regional economist at Singapore-based financial consultancy I.D.E.A. \par \par \uc2  "However, given Malaysia's record on structural reform and the risks of further regional ructions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to proceed cautiously. It seems likely that Bank Negara will cut gradually, observing the reaction of the market at each juncture," he said. \par \par \uc2  He expects the three-month interbank rate to fall to 9.0 percent by year-end. \par \par \uc2  In a major policy shift, Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on Friday cut the three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to 10.5 percent from 11 percent. \par \par \uc2  With inflation contained and the current account swinging into surplus, the "fundamental trends provide Malaysia with the room for a cautious easing of monetary policy to minimise the severity of the downturn in (the) domestic economy", it said. \par \par \uc2  The move marked a policy shift for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which for months had stood by tight money as the best way to defend the ringgit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pave the way for economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's gross domestic product shrank by 1.8 percent in the first quarter this year compared with the same period in 1997, its first contraction in 13 years. \par \par \uc2  The once-vibrant economy is officially forecast to contract by one to two percent in 1998, but analysts reckon that it could shrink by as much as four percent. \par \par \uc2  "Another (rate) cut before the end of the year is necessary to revive the economy. But I don't expect it to be so soon after the recent cut," said Chia Woon Khien, head of Asian research at Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad and Special Functions Minister Daim Zainuddin have campaigned for lower rates to help businesses survive the recession. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara also cited slowing money supply and credit growth as one of the reasons for the monetary easing. \par \par \uc2  Broad money, M3, expanded by 7.1 percent year-on-year in June against 9.6 percent in May, while annual lending growth slowed to 10.3 percent at the end of June from a year earlier, compared with 12 percent at the end of May. \par \par \uc2  On Monday and Tuesday, five banks cut their base lending rates to 12 percent from 12.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability was also prompting the authorities to cut rates. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit, which has lost nearly 40 percent of its value against the U.S. dollar since July last year, has kept to the 4.10-4.20 a dollar range in the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  "Cautious easing of monetary stance is seen as a positive move but only as long as inflation and the ringgit remain under control," Standard & Poor's MMS International said in a commentary. \par \par \uc2  "The next move hinges on forthcoming macro economic figures with another 100 basis points off the three-month rate by end-1998 likely," it said. ((Kuala Lumpur newsroom, +60 3 201-4813 fax +60 3 232-6752, kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du8401h5z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
