\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2 's/Klibor -2: Lower After Cut In  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rate \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1998\par 05:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--At the late morning fixing Monday, the most-watched three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (Klibor) was 10.55%, down marginally from 10.96% Friday. \par \par \uc2  Money market dealers said all rates are sharply lower Monday following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Friday announcement that it was reducing the three-month rate at which it lends to commercial banks to 10.5% from 11%, effective Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The lower rates are a direct reaction to Bank Negara cutting its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate," said a money market dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The new measure indicated that the country's policymakers have taken on a softer monetary policy to kick start the economy which have taken a severe beating since the collapse of regional Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July, 1998. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecast an cash flow surplus of 570 million ringgit (MYR) ($1=MYR4.1550) in the interbank market Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Negara Malaysia also said it wouldn't be conducting any money\par market tenders Monday.\par    Klibor Fixing          Monday        Friday\par    1-Month                10.47%        10.74%\par    3-Month                10.55%        10.96%\par    6-Month                10.83%        11.18%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Azizul Shamsuddin; 603 2925254; ashamsuddin@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0329GMT\p