\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  cuts  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  rate to 10.5 pct. \b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 13:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, July 31 (Reuters) - Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday that it will cut the three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to 10.5 percent from 11 percent effective August 3. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara Malaysia said in a statement that there was "room for a cautious easing of monetary policy to minimise the severity of the downturn in (the) domestic economy". \par \par \uc2  "The judgement is made that this monetary easing can be made without the risk of breaching the inflation objective," Bank Negara said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said there was an absence of inflationary pressures and the current account deficit was expected to turn around to a surplus position. \par \par \uc2  It said leading and lagging indicators such as sales and service tax collections, car sales, credit card spending and import demand were sharply down, and there was an absence of wage pressures. \par \par \uc2  "Similarly, the sharp downturn in equity prices and the softening of the property market have eliminated the inflationary potential of the asset markets," it said. \par \par \uc2  The growth of money supply and credit has slowed sharply to levels that are below the ceilings projected under the credit plan. \par \par \uc2  Inflation in developing countries was expected to remain subdued, with the moderation in petroleum prices supporting this trend, it said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that increases in the consumer and producer price indices essentially reflected the pass-through effects of the depreciation of the ringgit or were for certain specific items such as food due to supply factors. \par \par \uc2  "The adjustments resulting from the depreciation have, however, for the most part already been priced into current prices," it said. \par \par \uc2  "The price increases due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation have in effect been partially offset by dampening demand," it said, noting that Malaysia had one of the lowest rates of inflation in the region. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara said the improved current balance and long-term commitments in the form of foreign direct investment have supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . International reserves have hovered at about $20 billion, enough to cover 3.5 months of imports. \par \par \uc2  "These fundamental trends provide Malaysia with the room for a cautious easing of monetary policy to minimise the severity of the downturn in domestic policy," it said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last adjusted the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate in February when it raised it to 11 percent from 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  It also cut banks' statutory reserve requirement (SRR), or funds required to be kept interest-free with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to 10 percent from 13.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month, it cut the SRR again, to eight percent from 10. ((Kuala Lumpur newsroom, +60 3 201-4813 fax +60 3 232-6752, kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du7v013au\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
