\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Bank Negara cuts statutory reserves further. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Syed Azman \par \uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 15:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, June 26 (Reuters) - Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday announced a further cut in the statutory reserve requirement for banks that would release 8.0 billion ringgit ($2 billion) into the liquidity-strapped banking system. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara said it was cutting the requirement, or funds required to be kept interest-free with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to 8.0 percent of total deposits and other liabilities from 10 percent, from July 1. \par \par \uc2  It will be the second such cut this year. On February 16, Bank Negara lowered the requirement to 10 percent from 13.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said a sharp deceleration in monetary and credit growth and a slowdown in economic activity in the first half of the year prompted the latest move. \par \par \uc2  It earlier announced that broad M3 money growth had fallen to 9.6 percent year-on-year in May compared with 12.2 percent in April and 20.1 percent in the same month a year ago. \par \par \uc2  "Over the same (one-year) period, credit growth of the banking system slowed down from 30.4 percent at end-June 1997 to 12 percent at the end of May 1998," it said. \par \par \uc2  It said the reserve requirement cut was part of a series of measures that will be taken to ensure the "Malaysian economy does not spiral into a major economic slowdown". \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's gross domestic demand (GDP) sank 1.8 percent in the first quarter of this year, its first contraction since the 1985 recession. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts questioned whether the 8.0 billion ringgit would be enough to bring down rates, now hovering around 11 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The shortage itself is suspected to be much larger," said Sani Hamid, markets analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim said recently that 32 billion ringgit had flowed out of the banking system between January and May this year. \par \par \uc2  "The intention is of course to help provide funds for the system, thereby lower BLR, and help ailing corporates stay afloat," market consultancy firm I.D.E.A. said in a commentary. \par \par \uc2  "No doubt this will help provide support for the ailing corporate/banks, thereby the entire economy, but the cost of bailing out the banking sector is really exorbitant," it said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank Negara announcement came on the day Daim Zainuddin was sworn in as minister with special functions in charge of economic development. \par \par \uc2  Daim, a former finance minister, has spearheaded a drive to force banks to bring down lending rates. \par \par \uc2  His campaign, backed by Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad, has stoked tensions with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has cautioned that funds would flow out of the country, undercutting the already weak ringgit, if rates are pushed too low. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara said a two percentage point reduction in the reserve requirement would reduce the base lending rate of commercial banks by 0.21 percent and that of finance companies by 0.27 percent. \par \par \uc2  It said "the liquidity in the interbank market will be closely monitored and the three-month Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate will continue to remain unchanged". \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara's three-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is 11 percent. \par \par \uc2  Sani of MMS said he expected the SRR cut to have little near-term impact on the ringgit "as market accesses Daim and eyes possible fallout with Bank Negara over monetary policy". \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian unit fell below 4.00 per dollar on Friday, losing about 38 percent of its value against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since a regional financial crisis erupted last July. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q01ynf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
