\par\par \b \uc2  KL interbank rates largely steady in quiet trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1998\par 11:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, May 14 (Reuters) - Malaysian interbank rates were largely steady in quiet trading on Thursday with interest stirred only by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's morning tender to inject funds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Activity was thin as Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had indicated by recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it wanted the one-month rate at around 10.80 percent to 11.0 percent, and three-month at around 11.00 percent, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Negara gave the signal that they will give funds to anybody offering 10.80 and below for the one-month. They also got their objective to control 11 percent for the three-month," said a dealer at a Malaysian commercial bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier accepted bids at a weighted average rate of 10.89 percent for its one-month offer of 500 million ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The bids accepted were in the high/low range of 10.90 percent and 10.85 percent, respectively. \par \par \uc2  It said bids for 400 million ringgit of three-month money were accepted at an average 11.01 percent. Bids accepted were in the high/low range of 11.01 percent and 11.00 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was little activity to talk about other than the fund injections by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There was a one-month lender at 10.80 percent and three-month was traded at 11.0 percent, they said. \par \par \uc2  Banks now tailor their daily activities around the injections as they set the tone and direction for the markets, they said. \par \par \uc2  "It doesn't take much brains to do our job now," said a senior dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Players were also reluctant to take long-term positions due to uncertainties on the direction of interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the volatile Indonesian situation could increase pressure on the ringgit and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , thus forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep local rates high. ((Reme Ahmad, +60 3 201-4813 fax +60 3 232-6752, kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  *. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5e05err\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
