\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia shares, ringgit down at midday, off lows. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Azhar Sukri \par \uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1998\par 08:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, April 17 (Reuters) - Malaysian stocks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were battered early on Friday on growing concerns over the economy, but staged a partial recovery later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange's benchmark Composite Index ended the morning session 5.24 points, or 0.83 percent lower at 624.10, after falling over two percent earlier. \par \par \uc2  By 0453 GMT the ringgit stood at 3.7800/3.8000 per U.S. dollar, lower than the late Thursday level of 3.7300. It touched 3.8000 in morning trade. \par \par \uc2  "It's mostly been due to short covering action by some of the foreign houses, plus the fact that it's Friday so some of the local funds are propping up the market a bit," said a dealer at a local brokerage. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia has been hit by a slew of confidence-damaging factors this week. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday the Malaysian Institute for Economic Research said the country's business confidence index for the first quarter of 1998 fell by 8.6 points to 41.0, the lowest level in the index's 10-year history, from the previous quarter's 49.6 points. \par \par \uc2  The government reported a 2.2 percent decline in industrial production for February and an increase in inflation of 5.1 percent for March. \par \par \uc2  Investors also avoided Malaysian shares on fears that several more companies could be in trouble. Two listed companies have already been placed in receivership, with another facing a winding-up petition from one of its bankers. \par \par \uc2  Troubled construction group Ekran Bhd  was requoted on Friday morning, and immediately slumped 30 percent to its limit-down trading floor for the morning session. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday the group confirmed that it was pursuing a restructuring that would create a new majority owner at the firm. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia Airlines System Bhd  lost 13 cents to 2.85 ringgit, after losing 20 cents on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A newspaper report on Thursday said the group was planning a restructuring exercise which would allow its chairman to borrow funds against the company's aircraft and ultimately settle his personal debts. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think anyone with a brain would look at this stock at the moment. Why subject yourself to more pain," said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  "People are saying the index will go further down. One local fund is saying it may even go as low as 500," said another local share dealer. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to support the ringgit, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars at 3.80 ringgit through an agent bank. \par \par \uc2  "The agent is still offering dollars at 3.80 and this is capping the dollar's rise," a dealer with a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  No confirmation was available as Bank Negara does not normally comment on its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Ringgit is at risk for a pullback to the 4.00 (a dollar) level if 3.80 is broken," the European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian palm oil market rallied in early trading, extending its overnight bullish trend on the back of the weaker ringgit against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  By the end of morning session, Malaysia's benchmark third month July futures contract jumped 52 ringgit to 2,286 ringgit ($604.76) a tonne. \par \par \uc2  "Palm is again being driven by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . People came out to take advantage of a weak ringgit to hedge. It fell to the 3.80 level this morning," said a trader. \par \par \uc2  ($1=3.78 ringgit) ((Kuala Lumpur newsroom, +60 3 201-4813 fax +60 3 232-6752, kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4h076dc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
