\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  - zloty falls as NBP sells. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mike Dolan \par \uc2 879 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 15:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 24 (Reuters) - The recent rally in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was interrupted on Tuesday by National Bank of Poland (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the zloty and some disappointment at \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest economic package. \par \par \uc2  While sentiment toward high-yield local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in general remained robust, the NBP action and the temptation to take profits from recent sharp gains in emerging Asian units may mark a period of consolidation around the globe, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah and Philippine peso outperformed on the day in Asia, meantime, while the rouble continued to hold firm in the wake of Monday's dismissal of the Russian cabinet. \par \par \uc2  The zloty's retreat was the focus in European hours after the NBP sold zlotys for dollars on several occasions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated to 6.24 percent above its parity against a basket of officially-targeted \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus 6.78/54 percent above at the opening on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise decision on Monday to fix the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 6.51 percent above parity, well below prevailing market levels about 6.70 percent. \par \par \uc2  "There's been confusion over the zloty's direction over the past week, but the lower fixing on Monday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is saying enough is enough," said Miranda Xafa, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Salomon Smith Barney. \par \par \uc2  "Fighting inflation in Poland is clearly an important policy objective but opposition to excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength shows there is also some worries about the external accounts." \par \par \uc2  The past week has been a roller-coaster for the zloty. \par \par \uc2  The volatility started with a sudden bout of profit taking last Wednesday after investment firm Goldman Sachs recommended it was time to cut long positions. \par \par \uc2  The zloty recovered its losses by Friday, however, and then soared to as high as 7.50 percent after reported comments, later denied, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was happy with recent strength. \par \par \uc2  "The sheer volatility of the zloty over the past week will probably be enough to take the pure \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation out of the market, but the yield story is still attractive unless you think there is going to be a complete collapse," said a trader at a U.S. investment firm. \par \par \uc2  The Russian rouble held firm following President Boris Yeltsin's decision to dismiss Prime Minister Viktor Chernomyrdin and his cabinet on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the underlying uncertainty of Russian politics had been highlighted again, but it looked as if a reconstituted cabinet would lean toward reformers rather than signal any great change in economic policy. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Europe, the Czech crown was steady about 18.61 per mark, with chart analysts saying there was strong trendline resistance on any uptick above 18.64. \par \par \uc2  In more exotic European markets, the collapse of the Belarussian rouble stole the show. \par \par \uc2  Local dealers said the Belarussian unit plummeted on the interbank market to as low as 64,000-69,000 per dollar against 52,000-54,000 per dollar late last week. \par \par \uc2  In Moscow, the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recommended that Russian citizens refrain from trading the Belarussian unit and said it ceased quoting an official rate against the Russian rouble. \par \par \uc2  This was in response to the Belarussian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on Monday to stop foreigners trading its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Belarussian rouble was at 45,000-47,000 to the dollar at the beginning of this year. \par \par \uc2  In Asia, the Malaysian ringgit erased much of Monday's gains amid profit-taking and some disappointment that a package of new economic measures announced by Deputy Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim fell short of easing restrictions on foreign investment. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MARKETS SNAPSHOT \par \par \uc2  The following is a snapshot of emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  ASIA \par \par \uc2  * Indonesian rupiah 8,550 per dollar bid vs 8,900 late in London on Monday. \par \par \uc2  * Malaysian ringgit at 3.64 per dollar from 3.535 per dollar on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Thai baht 38.60 per dollar vs 38.40. \par \par \uc2  Philippine peso 37.00 per dollar vs 37.63. \par \par \uc2  * South Korean won 1,374 versus 1,363 Monday. \par \par \uc2  * Singapore dollar 1.6100 per dollar versus 1.5995. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan dollar at 32.65 vs 32.70. \par \par \uc2  * Indian rupee at 39.40 per dollar versus 39.50. \par \par \uc2  EUROPE \par \par \uc2  * Russian rouble at 6.0835 per dollar bid vs 6.0810. Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily bid/offer rates at 6.0780/6.1200 versus 6.0760/6.1180 Monday. \par \par \uc2  * Zloty about 6.20 percent above basket parity from 6.78/54 percent at the opening. \par \par \uc2  Mark/Czech crown at 18.619 bid compared with 18.626 Monday. \par \par \uc2  * Slovak crown 2.00 percent below basket parity versus 1.80 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Hungarian forint at 2.24 percent above its basket parity versus 2.25 percent Monday. \par \par \uc2  * Ukrainian hryvnia 2.0368 per dollar versus 2.0385. \par \par \uc2  Romanian leu at 8490 per dollar versus 8370. \par \par \uc2  AFRICA \par \par \uc2  * South African rand at 4.9745 per dollar vs 4.9783. \par \par \uc2  Kenyan shilling 60.0 vs 59.90. \par \par \uc2  LATIN AMERICA \par \par \uc2  * Mexican peso at 8.545 per dollar vs 8.535. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's real at 1.1349 per dollar bid vs 1.1342. \par \par \uc2  ((London Newsroom +44 171 542 5110 fax 583 7239, uk.emergingmarkets.news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3o08t3g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
