\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Up Slightly Vs Dollar On Stk Mkt Gains \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 1998\par 04:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit (MYR) was slightly higher against the U.S. dollar in early trading Monday as players look to the advancing stock market for indication of the ringgit's direction. \par \par \uc2  Around 0239 GMT (9:39 p.m. EST), the dollar was at MYR3.8350, down marginally from MYR3.8544 late Friday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traded between MYR3.8400 and MYR3.8700 so far this morning. \par \par \uc2  Though the correlation isn't direct, dealers report that foreign funds flowing into Asian equities, including Malaysia's, are boosting demand for local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they convert dollar holdings to pick up local stocks. \par \par \uc2  Currently, the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange is at 753.13 points, up 24.94 points, or 3.4% from Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Market reaction has also been muted to the weekend's cut in the statutory reserve requirement of Malaysian banks from 13.5% to 10%. The extra liquidity pumped into the market is seen balanced by the hike in Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to 11% from 10% and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's pledge to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less in the money market. \par \par \uc2  A Hong Kong-based dealer said 'it's too early say whether the market has now stabilized or that there's (a solid) change in the trend).' He noted that spill-over effects from any Indonesian political instability could hit regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But he added that if ringgit sentiment continues to strengthen, the next level to look for would be MYR3.7700/dollar. A Singapore-based dealer thought the ringgit would meet resistance at MYR3.8000. Both dealers said ringgit support would be found at MYR3.9000. \par \par \uc2  Market volume, they say, will remain low. \par \par \uc2  -By Charles Roth; 603-292-5254; croth@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-02-98 \par \par \uc2  0321GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du29012kh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
